# PART 1 — How Code Becomes an App

Before learning syntax, you need to understand what actually happens when you press "Run".

```
YOUR CODE (JavaScript/TypeScript)
         │
         ▼
    Metro Bundler
    (reads all your .js/.ts files,
     bundles them into one big file)
         │
         ▼
    JavaScript Engine
    (Hermes on Android, JavaScriptCore on iOS)
    (runs your JS logic)
         │
         ▼
    React Native Bridge
    (translates JS commands into
     native platform calls)
         │
    ┌────┴────┐
    ▼         ▼
 Android      iOS
 (Java/      (Swift/
  Kotlin)     ObjC)
    │              │
    ▼              ▼
 Real native    Real native
 Android UI     iOS UI
```

Your JavaScript never directly touches the screen. It sends instructions through the bridge. React Native converts `<View>` → `android.widget.FrameLayout` on Android, and `UIView` on iOS. This is why the same code runs on both platforms.

