## Why does `android/` exist if you write JavaScript?

Because React Native is not a web app. When you install a package like `react-native-svg`, it has two parts:

```
react-native-svg/
├── src/          ← JavaScript part (the API you use in code)
├── android/      ← Android-specific native code (Java/Kotlin)
└── ios/          ← iOS-specific native code (Swift/ObjC)
```

The JavaScript calls the native code through the bridge. This is why you need to run `pod install` on iOS — it compiles the native iOS part of the library.

