# PART 6 — Flexbox Layout (the only layout system in RN)

React Native uses Flexbox for ALL positioning. There is no CSS grid, no floats, no absolute positioning by default.

```tsx
// CRITICAL: In React Native, flexDirection defaults to 'column'
// In CSS (web), flexDirection defaults to 'row'

// Centering something — the most common pattern
<View style={{ flex: 1, justifyContent: 'center', alignItems: 'center' }}>
  <Text>I am perfectly centered</Text>
</View>

// flex: 1 means "take all available space"
// justifyContent controls the MAIN axis (column = vertical by default)
// alignItems controls the CROSS axis (column = horizontal by default)

// Row layout — side by side
<View style={{ flexDirection: 'row', justifyContent: 'space-between' }}>
  <Text>Left</Text>
  <Text>Right</Text>
</View>

// Proportional sizing with flex
<View style={{ flex: 1, flexDirection: 'row' }}>
  <View style={{ flex: 1, backgroundColor: 'red' }}  />  // takes 1/3
  <View style={{ flex: 2, backgroundColor: 'blue' }} />  // takes 2/3
</View>
```

