# PART 11 — Sequelize ORM

An ORM (Object Relational Mapper) lets you work with database records as JavaScript objects instead of writing raw SQL.

```js
// WITHOUT ORM — raw SQL:
const result = await pool.query(
  'SELECT * FROM "Tasks" WHERE "userId" = $1 ORDER BY "createdAt" DESC',
  [userId]
);

// WITH Sequelize ORM — JavaScript:
const tasks = await db.Task.findAll({
  where: { userId: userId },
  order: [['createdAt', 'DESC']],
});
// Both do exactly the same thing under the hood
```

## Model definition

```js
// A model is a JavaScript class that maps to a database table
class Task extends Model {}

Task.init({
  // Each property maps to a database column
  id: {
    type: DataTypes.UUID,
    primaryKey: true,
    defaultValue: DataTypes.UUIDV4, // auto-generates UUID
  },
  name: {
    type: DataTypes.STRING,   // VARCHAR(255)
    allowNull: false,         // NOT NULL constraint
  },
  isActive: {
    type: DataTypes.BOOLEAN,
    defaultValue: true,
  },
  description: DataTypes.TEXT, // shorthand when no extra config needed
}, {
  sequelize,      // the database connection
  tableName: 'Tasks',
  modelName: 'Task',
});
```

## The 4 CRUD operations

```js
// CREATE — INSERT INTO
const task = await db.Task.create({
  name: 'Build the API',
  userId: 'uuid-123',
});
console.log(task.id); // auto-generated UUID

// READ — SELECT
const all   = await db.Task.findAll();                    // all rows
const one   = await db.Task.findByPk('uuid-123');         // by primary key
const first = await db.Task.findOne({ where: { name: 'Build' } }); // first match

// With conditions:
const active = await db.Task.findAll({
  where: { isActive: true, userId: 'abc' },
  order: [['createdAt', 'DESC']],
  limit: 10,
  include: [{ model: db.User, as: 'owner' }], // JOIN
});

// UPDATE — UPDATE SET
task.name = 'Updated name';
task.isActive = false;
await task.save();    // only saves changed fields

// Or update without fetching first:
await db.Task.update(
  { isActive: false },               // what to set
  { where: { userId: 'uuid-123' } }  // which rows
);

// DELETE — DELETE FROM
await task.destroy();

// Or delete without fetching:
await db.Task.destroy({ where: { id: 'uuid-123' } });
```

